// LocalAgentDefinition ADR-0037 decision 1: a local agent is an AGENTS.md file in a desktop workspace, read by the D0 project-instructions loader (libs/rust/local-tools/src/project_instructions.rs). The loader is the authority on its caps and refusals; this schema states them so a client can check a file before it asks the approval bridge to write it. Caps the loader enforces on every read: the file name is AGENTS.md (matched case-insensitively, the exact spelling wins); all AGENTS.md text one turn reads, root and nested together, is at most 32768 bytes, and text past the cap is not read; a symlinked file or folder is not read; a path the workspace denies is not read. A nested AGENTS.md (scope other than `root`) applies to a turn that references a path under that folder, in addition to the root file.
